      "id": "xy9cbha",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Ions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8l8k2zw",
      "content": "Ions are charged particles."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7tgr0ta",
      "content": "Cation: Positively charged ion (Na+)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gvt6ccu",
      "content": "Anion: Negatively charged ion (Cl−)."
    },
    {
      "id": "pi9k1ts",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Molecular Mass"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jl1dfg3",
      "content": "Molecular mass = Sum of atomic masses of all atoms in a molecule."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "spp9dos",
      "content": "Example: H2O = (2×1) + 16 = 18 u"
    },
    {
      "id": "pi1zjbd",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Structure of Atom"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pya6ti3",
      "content": "Electron discovered by J.J. Thomson."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lblmjlf",
      "content": "Proton discovered by Rutherford."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u11zls0",
      "content": "Neutron discovered by James Chadwick."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "tb81yqh",
      "content": "Rutherford Model: Nucleus at centre, electrons revolve around it."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6w5ylbc",
      "content": "Bohr Model: Electrons revolve in fixed shells (K, L, M, N)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bk3lkch",
      "content": "Maximum electrons in shell = 2n² (where n = shell number)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pxyhriq",
      "content": "Maximum electrons in outermost shell = 8."
    },
